---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BuyingGuidance from '../components/BuyingGuidance.astro';
import Btn from '../components/Btn.astro';
---
<Base title="Planning Your First AI Automation Project | NextGenius" description="Understand who NextGenius helps, what to bring to discovery, how project scope and estimates are agreed, and what to check before an AI automation build.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="Getting started" title="From first conversation to a working system." lead="Know what to bring, how we choose an approach and what to look for in a proposal for AI, automation or software development.">
    <div class="btns"><Btn href="/contact/" label="Book a free consultation" /><a class="tlink" href="/contact/">Ask a project question</a></div>
  </PageHero>
  <BuyingGuidance showGuideLink={false} />
  <section class="sec white" id="prepare"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Prepare for discovery</p><h2>You bring the business context. We explore the options.</h2></div><div><p>Your initial consultation is free and usually takes 30–45 minutes. We discuss your goals, current tools and whether NextGenius can help. There is no obligation to proceed. A detailed assessment or prototype is scoped and priced separately before work begins.</p><ul class="guide-list"><li>The task and who currently owns it.</li><li>The tools involved: inbox, calendar, booking system or customer records.</li><li>Approximate task volume and time spent today.</li><li>Common exceptions and approval steps.</li><li>Priorities, budget constraints and any deadline.</li></ul><p>A finished technical brief is not needed. Keep examples general and leave out confidential information.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="sec wrap"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Choose a starting point that fits.</h2><p>A custom AI build is one option. The useful choice depends on your workflow, information and existing software.</p></div><div class="guide-grid"><div><h3>Use what you already have</h3><p>If a built-in feature or simple automation handles the task, begin there. A repeatable process with clear rules may not need AI.</p></div><div><h3>Assess an uncertain workflow</h3><p>When data access, system connections or the business case are unclear, scope a focused assessment before committing to implementation.</p></div><div><h3>Prototype a narrow use case</h3><p>Test a small version on representative examples, with agreed measures and staff review. Use what you learn to decide whether to proceed.</p></div><div><h3>Plan a defined build</h3><p>If the requirements and integration access are already understood, agree design, implementation, testing, handover and support milestones.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="sec white"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Questions to settle before paid work begins.</h2><div><ul class="guide-list"><li>What is included, excluded and delivered at each milestone?</li><li>Which accounts, permissions and subscriptions will be needed, and who pays for them?</li><li>What test examples and acceptance criteria determine whether the work is ready?</li><li>Who owns custom work, maintains source information and handles failed workflows?</li><li>What documentation, training, support and exit arrangements are included?</li></ul><div class="btns"><a class="tlink" href="/blog/choosing-your-first-automation-workflow/">Choose your first workflow</a><a class="tlink" href="/blog/ai-assistant-pilot-checklist/">Plan an assistant pilot</a></div></div></div></section>
</Base>
